  ---                                                                                                                                                                                         
  BasketTube — AI Basketball Game Analyzer                                                                                                                                                    
                                                                                                                                                                                              
  Overview                                                                                                                                                                                    
                                                                                                                                                                                              
  Offline pipeline for semantic analysis of basketball broadcast footage. Two parallel tracks: commentary-based Q&A and vision-based action retrieval. Both use the same game footage and     
  Whisper transcription as a shared foundation.                                                                                                                                               
                                                                                                                                                                                              
  ---             
  Shared Foundation
                   
  - Input: Single game video (game_1.mp4, Lakers vs Warriors)
  - Transcription: Whisper medium (local) → subtitles.csv — 1153 segments, frame-aligned at 30fps                                                                                             
  - Frame extraction: Full-resolution frames (1918×1078) at 30fps → game_1/frames/                                                                                                            
                                                                                                                                                                                              
  ---                                                                                                                                                                                         
  Track 1 — Commentary-Based Q&A                                                                                                                                                              
                                
  Goal: Answer natural language questions about player performance using commentary as evidence.
                                                                                                                                                                                              
  Architecture (RAG pipeline):
  1. CLIP text encoder embeds all 1153 subtitle segments → embedding index                                                                                                                    
  2. User query → CLIP text encoder → nearest-neighbor retrieval (top-K)                                                                                                                      
  3. Retrieved subtitle chunks → LLM synthesis → structured answer      
  4. M3U playlist generated for matching video segments (VLC-playable)                                                                                                                        
                                                                                                                                                                                              
  Current state: Working (player_performance.py), using Sonnet API for synthesis.                                                                                                             
                                                                                                                                                                                              
  Next step — Teacher-Student Distillation:                                                                                                                                                   
  - Teacher: Sonnet (generate_dataset.py) — receives 3 frames + subtitle, returns structured 4-section response (DIRECT RESPONSE / SUMMARY / EVIDENCE / DISCLAIMER)                           
  - Dataset: ~1153 entries, each with 3 base64 frames + commentary + Sonnet response                                                                                                          
  - Student: PaliGemma-3B fine-tuned via QLoRA on generated dataset (finetune_vlm.py)
  - Goal: local inference with no API calls at runtime                                                                                                                                        
                                                                                                                                                                                              
  ---                                                                                                                                                                                         
  Track 2 — Vision-Based Action Retrieval                                                                                                                                                     
                                                                                                                                                                                              
  Goal: Retrieve video moments matching a text query using visual content, not commentary.
                                                                                                                                                                                              
  Architecture (VLM):                                                                                                                                                                         
  Frame t-start ┐                                                                                                                                                                             
  Frame t-mid   ├→ frozen CLIP ViT-L/14 (1024-dim each) → concat (3072-dim) → ProjectionLayer → 768-dim                                                                                       
  Frame t-end   ┘                                                                                                                                                                             
                                                            ↕ CosineEmbeddingLoss                                                                                                             
                                                CLIP text encoder (subtitle text) → 768-dim                                                                                                   
                                                                                                                                                                                              
  - 3 frames sampled per subtitle segment: start/mid/end of a context window centered on the subtitle                                                                                         
  - CONTEXT_SECONDS controls window spread — 5 models trained (3s, 5s, 10s, 15s, 20s)                                                                                                         
  - At query time: CLIP text encoder embeds query → cosine similarity against visual index → top-K results → M3U playlist                                                                     
                                                                                                                                                                                              
  Training results: Cosine similarity 0.54–0.64 after 9 epochs; loss plateau at ~0.408 (ceiling for single-game dataset)                                                                      
                                                                                                                                                                                              
